  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES (still unmeasured; no corpus A/B found in tracker or lab notebook; the 09-25 P2 review said the same).\n\nConstruct still ships: js_ts.py:6138-6194 (assignment_expression branch, call_construct=\"assignment\", added 804a402089 WI-dosuh); JS_ASSIGNABLE_ROWS js_ts.py:1046 = WebSocket{onmessage,onclose,...}, EventSource{onmessage,...}, BroadcastChannel, XMLHttpRequest, net/dgram Socket, dns.Resolver.\nFixture (app.js: `ws = new WebSocket(u); ws.onmessage = function(ev){ exec(ev.data) }`; `es = new EventSource(u); es.onmessage = handle` where handle never calls exec; `ws.binaryType = \"blob\"`): survey emits 2 assignment edges (WebSocket.onmessage, EventSource.onmessage), none for binaryType. verify-claims with docs/example-claims/generic-taint-claims.yaml: untrusted-input-no-subprocess VIOLATED, \"2 source->sink pair(s)\", sources EventSource.onmessage + WebSocket.onmessage -> child_process.exec, both anchored on `start`. The EventSource pair is FALSE (the named handler never reaches exec): the precision concern in this row reproduces on a 12-line fixture, for the NAMED-handler spelling too, not only the inline one.\n\nUpdates since filing:\n- Cohort repos are on this box: ~/whole_bunch_of_repos/{vscode (186M), nextjs (325M), podman-desktop (317M)}.\n- Cheap grep (NOT the instrument; spelling count only) for `.on(message|close|error|open) =`: vscode 56, nextjs 128, podman-desktop 0. Dominant receivers are uncatalogued (mainWindow.onerror, port/worker/self.onmessage, link.onerror). Files with `new WebSocket(`/`new EventSource(`: vscode 2, nextjs 5. Expect a small emitted count; the row's \"browser-facing repo\" caveat applies.\n- Sink set moved: WI-nokab (done) shipped code-/DOM-injection sinks, so the precision arm now has more co-location targets than at filing.\n- Open neighbours that change what an A/B would measure: WI-vubal (named handler gets no edge), WI-ritog (arrival-scope seeding), WI-vogos (net_listen retag). Measuring before WI-ritog lands measures the co-location shape it would remove; consider isbefore WI-ritog -> this row.\nCorpus A/B itself not run (out of scope for this check)."  # d6c4
- op: update  # 74ea
