  set:  # 74ea
    description: "UNMEASURED, AND FILED RATHER THAN ASSUMED EITHER WAY.\n\nWI-dosuh (PR #903) made `ws.onmessage = h` emit a registration edge (js_ts.py\n~6138-6194, call_construct=\"assignment\", for the receiver/property pairs in\nJS_ASSIGNABLE_ROWS ~1046: WebSocket, EventSource, BroadcastChannel,\nXMLHttpRequest, net/dgram Socket, dns.Resolver), and the construct turned out\nNOT to be inert: on a fixture it produces a live `untrusted-input-no-subprocess`\nviolation, correctly. What was NEVER measured is what it does to a real corpus.\n\nWHY THAT MATTERS IN BOTH DIRECTIONS.\n  - RECALL: WebSocket/SSE handler assignment is the ordinary spelling in browser\n    code. Every site was previously invisible. How many are there, and how many\n    reach a sink?\n  - PRECISION: the source is anchored on the ENCLOSING function of the\n    assignment, so ANY sink in that function co-locates with the source on the\n    structural arm. This holds for the inline-handler spelling AND the named one:\n    on a fixture, `es.onmessage = handle` (handle never calls exec) beside an\n    inline `ws.onmessage` handler that does yields 2 source->sink pairs, the\n    EventSource one false. The co-location FP fires for addEventListener\n    identically, so the shape is pre-existing — but \"pre-existing shape\" is not\n    \"same volume\". This change adds a new population of sources the shape can\n    act on, and WI-nokab (done) has since added code-/DOM-injection sinks, so\n    there are more sinks to co-locate with. The added volume is unknown.\n\nWHAT TO MEASURE. An A/B over the analyzer change (a survey per arm — an analyzer\nchange MOVES the survey, so io-boundaries/verify-claims alone are not enough),\none session and one XDG_CACHE_HOME per arm, subject blob asserted at BEGIN and\nEND. Report per repo:\n  1. count of `call_construct: assignment` edges emitted;\n  2. how many reach a catalogue row (the RECALL figure) vs how many are merely\n     slotted — these are DIFFERENT numbers and conflating them is the WI-kikar\n     892-vs-278 error;\n  3. `calls_total` in both arms — it must be identical, since this only ADDS\n     edges and takes nothing from an already-resolved symbol;\n  4. verify-claims verdict deltas, and for EVERY new finding, adjudicate it\n     against source as true or false. Do not report a finding count alone.\n\nCOHORT. The JS repos already in the pool: vscode, nextjs, podman-desktop\n(~/whole_bunch_of_repos/). These are Node-heavy; the WebSocket/EventSource\nsurface is a BROWSER surface, so a null result on this cohort may reflect cohort\nchoice rather than the change. A spelling grep (not the instrument) for\n`.on(message|close|error|open) =` finds vscode 56, nextjs 128, podman-desktop 0,\ndominated by receivers with no catalogue row (window/img/link .onerror,\nport/worker/self .onmessage); files constructing a WebSocket/EventSource:\nvscode 2, nextjs 5. Expect a small emitted count; say so explicitly if it comes\nback near zero, and consider whether a browser-facing repo belongs in the pool.\n\nRELATED (open; each changes what the A/B would measure): WI-vubal (a named\nhandler assigned to a property gets no edge to the handler), WI-ritog (seed taint\nat the arrival scope — would remove the co-location shape), WI-vogos (JS\nnet_listen retag).\n\nDO NOT CLOSE THIS BY RE-RUNNING A GREEN DEEP CYCLE. DEEP band metrics are\nhealthy-range metrics, not deltas; a green cycle validates nothing here.\n\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # 74ea
