  message: "MEASURED 2026-10-01 (WI-zohuk agent, worktree ~/hg_wt/zohuk). Branch jgstern-agent/docs/zohuk-handler-assignment-measurement, commit ac2a5479a2 (docs only: docs/measurements/0030-js-handler-assignment-corpus-delta.md + index row). Not pushed. Raw data and instrument: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_09302026/zohuk/.\n\nMETHOD (as this item prescribes): arm A = dev 8cfcab7b07 with JS_ASSIGNABLE_ROWS emptied in an overlay copy of the mainstream sources (js_ts.py blob d8ca8124; the name is read only by the emission branch); arm B = dev as committed (blob 11d17da8). Per arm and repo: survey, verify-claims (generic-taint-claims.yaml; default and --include-non-production-sources), io-boundaries (default and --include-tests); imported blob and subject HEAD + porcelain digest asserted at BEGIN and END; one XDG_CACHE_HOME per arm.\n\nPER REPO (the item's four numbers):\n  vscode   emitted 0; calls 342,838 = 342,838; 0 verdict changes; 0 situations new/lost/changed.\n  lila     emitted 0; calls 82,681 = 82,681; 0; 0.   (added as a browser-facing repo; its ws is bound by const ws = (this.ws = new WebSocket(u)), which the typing does not see)\n  argo-cd  emitted 1 (PRODUCTION, ui/src/app/shared/services/requests.ts:92, EventSource.onmessage), reaches its row (net_recv) in both io-boundaries runs; calls 49,104 -> 49,105; 0 verdict changes; 0 situations new/lost/changed.\n  nestjs   emitted 2 (both test files), reach their row only with --include-tests; calls 20,658 -> 20,660; 0; 0.\n  nest     (second clone of nestjs) same 2 lines; 0; 0.\n  nextjs   NOT MEASURED by survey: arm B stopped by pid at 3 h 05 min (vscode trial predicted 2.7-3.1 h per arm; the run coordinator's rule stops a pair over 6 h). Analyzer census: 1 emitted edge, test file subscribeToHMR.ts:39.\n  podman-desktop  not surveyed: 0 emitted in the analyzer census, so the arms cannot differ (checked empirically on vscode and lila, the two other zero-emission repos).\nNon-destruction held on all five surveyed repos: arm A's edge multiset (order-independent digest over every edge) equals arm B's minus exactly the emitted edges; the digest control was mutated and went red.\nRECALL: 4 distinct emitted sites across a 38-repo analyzer census, all 4 correct on reading the source; 1 production. A spelling census by receiver binding: 4 of 21 typable handler sites emitted; the 17 misses are receiver-binding gaps (WI-ponid; notes there).\nPRECISION: zero new findings in either configuration, so the population to adjudicate is EMPTY. That is not a 100% precision figure.\nVERDICT GATE: on a fixture (const ws = new WebSocket(u); ws.onmessage = function(ev){console.log(ev.data)}; plus an untyped sink.write), the construct flips 7 of 7 generic claims from confirmed_with_caveats to inconclusive: method_starved_modules counts WebSocket as called and starved, because \"assignment\" is not in the module's kind set and onmessage is method-kind. 0 occurrences on the surveyed repos (each also has a method-stamped call into the same module, e.g. eventSource.close()). Noted on WI-dapap (its remedy (2) predicted this member inert) and WI-bobuf (sixth classified-yet-starved instance). Not fixed here.\nNOT ESTABLISHED: nextjs; the construct's recall after WI-ponid; anything after WI-ritog / WI-vubal / WI-vogos land. Tests: targeted smart-test 287 passed, 0 failed (docs-only change, no changed sources)."  # f993
